      "id": 16,
      "options": {
        "content": "Use `trace_id` from a Policy completion log to open the matching Tempo trace. Request panels count the private HTTP edge only (`insurance_hub_service_transport=\"http\"`); the internal gRPC hop is excluded so requests are not counted twice. Separate the failing boundary before acting: upstream RPC failures show as `UNAVAILABLE`, `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED`, `INTERNAL` or `UNKNOWN` on the Product `GetProduct` or Pricing `CalculatePrice` `rpc_method`; PostgreSQL loss shows database readiness 0 with lifecycle operations ending `UNAVAILABLE`; Kafka loss shows Kafka publisher readiness 0 or publication `error` outcomes. Database readiness 0 with `policy event publication deferred` warnings and no publication errors is delayed outbox publication, not a Kafka failure; check pending intents with the read-only outbox query in the runbook. Legitimate idle time has zero request and publication rates, present Go runtime samples and readiness 1. An available deployment without a runtime sample is missing telemetry. Telemetry delivery panels describe the shared Alloy pipeline, not Policy: rising drop, failure, lag or queue signals indicate collection failure. Labels remain bounded and never expose policy, offer or customer data, amounts, credentials, topics, arbitrary errors or trace IDs.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Investigation workflow",
      "type": "text"
    }
